{"text": "[deadpan] Four hundred dollars... ... for storage.\nThe Wall Street Journal estimates it cost Apple about forty-two bucks.\nThat's the jump to one terabyte on an iPhone 17 Pro.\nWhy do we pay it? Look at the menu.\nBase iPad. Three sizes. Three prices.\nYour eyes skip the cheapest... dodge the priciest... and land right in the middle.\nPsychologists call that pull the compromise effect.\nIts famous cousin is the decoy.\nThe Economist once offered print-only for the same price as print plus web.\nNobody took print-only. But the bundle jumped from thirty-two percent... to eighty-four.\n[rewind] Wait. Here's the twist.\nWhen researchers retested decoys with real products, the effect mostly... vanished.\nEleven solid results out of ninety-one tries.\n[sarcastic] So maybe the trick isn't in your head. It's in the price gap.\nSources are in the pinned comment. Because that upgrade button still says...", "model": "eleven_v3", "voice": "8Ln42OXYupYsag45MAUy", "alignment": {"characters": ["[", "d", "e", "a", "d", "p", "a", "n", "]", " ", "F", "o", "u", "r", " ", "h", "u", "n", "d", "r", "e", "d", " ", "d", "o", "l", "l", "a", "r", "s", ".", ".", ".", " ", ".", ".", ".", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "s", "t", "o", "r", "a", "g", "e", ".", "\n", "T", "h", "e", " ", "W", "a", "l", "l", " ", "S", "t", "r", "e", "e", "t", " ", "J", "o", "u", "r", "n", "a", "l", " ", "e", "s", "t", "i", "m", "a", "t", "e", "s", " ", "i", "t", " ", "c", "o", "s", "t", " ", "A", "p", "p", "l", "e", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "f", "o", "r", "t", "y", "-", "t", "w", "o", " ", "b", "u", "c", "k", "s", ".", "\n", "T", "h", "a", "t", "'", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "j", "u", "m", "p", " ", "t", "o", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "t", "e", "r", "a", "b", "y", "t", "e", " ", "o", "n", " ", "a", "n", " ", "i", "P", "h", "o", "n", "e", " ", "1", "7", " ", "P", "r", "o", ".", "\n", "W", "h", "y", " ", "d", "o", " ", "w", "e", " ", "p", "a", "y", " ", "i", "t", "?", " ", "L", "o", "o", "k", " ", "a